 "lq": [
  {
   "_id": 12403,
   "ANSWER": "<ul>\n\t<li data-end=\"3087\" data-start=\"2917\">\n\t<p data-end=\"2946\" data-start=\"2919\"><strong data-end=\"2944\" data-start=\"2919\">Scheduling Mechanism: 20%</strong></p>\n\n\t<ul data-end=\"3087\" data-start=\"2949\">\n\t\t<li data-end=\"3023\" data-start=\"2949\">\n\t\t<p data-end=\"3023\" data-start=\"2951\">RR uses a fixed time quantum and cycles through processes (time-based)</p>\n\t\t</li>\n\t\t<li data-end=\"3087\" data-start=\"3026\">\n\t\t<p data-end=\"3087\" data-start=\"3028\">Priority assigns CPU based on priority values (value-based)</p>\n\t\t</li>\n\t</ul>\n\t</li>\n\t<li data-end=\"3278\" data-start=\"3089\">\n\t<p data-end=\"3119\" data-start=\"3091\"><strong data-end=\"3117\" data-start=\"3091\">Fairness &amp; Starvation:&nbsp;</strong><strong data-end=\"2944\" data-start=\"2919\">20%</strong></p>\n\n\t<ul data-end=\"3278\" data-start=\"3122\">\n\t\t<li data-end=\"3180\" data-start=\"3122\">\n\t\t<p data-end=\"3180\" data-start=\"3124\">RR is fair (equal CPU share), low chance of starvation</p>\n\t\t</li>\n\t\t<li data-end=\"3278\" data-start=\"3183\">\n\t\t<p data-end=\"3278\" data-start=\"3185\">Priority can lead to starvation, especially for low-priority processes (unless aging is used)</p>\n\t\t</li>\n\t</ul>\n\t</li>\n\t<li data-end=\"3427\" data-start=\"3280\">\n\t<p data-end=\"3300\" data-start=\"3282\"><strong data-end=\"3298\" data-start=\"3282\">Suitability:&nbsp;</strong><strong data-end=\"2944\" data-start=\"2919\">20%</strong></p>\n\n\t<ul data-end=\"3427\" data-start=\"3303\">\n\t\t<li data-end=\"3344\" data-start=\"3303\">\n\t\t<p data-end=\"3344\" data-start=\"3305\">RR: time-sharing, interactive systems</p>\n\t\t</li>\n\t\t<li data-end=\"3427\" data-start=\"3347\">\n\t\t<p data-end=\"3427\" data-start=\"3349\">Priority: real-time systems where critical processes must be executed promptly</p>\n\t\t</li>\n\t</ul>\n\t</li>\n\t<li data-end=\"3602\" data-start=\"3429\">\n\t<p data-end=\"3470\" data-start=\"3431\"><strong data-end=\"3468\" data-start=\"3431\">Waiting/Turnaround Time Handling:&nbsp;</strong><strong data-end=\"2944\" data-start=\"2919\">20%</strong></p>\n\n\t<ul data-end=\"3602\" data-start=\"3473\">\n\t\t<li data-end=\"3536\" data-start=\"3473\">\n\t\t<p data-end=\"3536\" data-start=\"3475\">RR: waiting time depends on number of processes and quantum</p>\n\t\t</li>\n\t\t<li data-end=\"3602\" data-start=\"3539\">\n\t\t<p data-end=\"3602\" data-start=\"3541\">Priority: variable based on process priority and arrival time</p>\n\t\t</li>\n\t</ul>\n\t</li>\n\t<li data-end=\"3720\" data-start=\"3604\">\n\t<p data-end=\"3621\" data-start=\"3606\"><strong data-end=\"3619\" data-start=\"3606\">Examples:&nbsp;</strong><strong data-end=\"2944\" data-start=\"2919\">20%</strong></p>\n\n\t<ul data-end=\"3720\" data-start=\"3624\">\n\t\t<li data-end=\"3720\" data-start=\"3624\">\n\t\t<p data-end=\"3720\" data-start=\"3626\">Reference examples from documents (RR: P1, P2, P3 with Q=4ms; Priority: P1&ndash;P5 with priorities)</p>\n\t\t</li>\n\t</ul>\n\t</li>\n</ul>\n",
   "COURSE_CODE": "21CSC202J",
   "LEVEL": 4,
